{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py","reason":"Wrap the local web-search tool so DDGSException is caught at rebar's own boundary: an empty list for the indistinguishable 'No results found.' case, and a single WEB_SEARCH_UNAVAILABLE marker record otherwise. Neither branch re-raises, so a web-search outcome can no longer void an entire plan review."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T1.md","reason":"Add the reader-side anchor the marker needs. Line 10 currently instructs T1 to treat all search-result text as untrusted data and never as direction, which would make the marker's in-band rule inert. Add a narrow clause recognising a rebar-issued tool-failure notice, gated on a single record with title exactly WEB_SEARCH_UNAVAILABLE and an empty href, granting no authority beyond reporting prior art as unverified."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_web_tool_gating.py","reason":"Red/green tests: DDGSException('No results found.') returns an empty list rather than raising; DDGSException('backend exploded') returns one marker whose title, href and body match; both branches validate against TypeAdapter(list[DuckDuckGoResult]); web_search_capabilities installs rebar's wrapper rather than pydantic-ai's raw tool. No live network."}]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1789956987083011997,"uuid":"706ce114-2f92-4678-9141-5b1da516bb73"}